Efficiency is how productively a firm utilizes its assets relative to its revenue
and its profits. Southwest Airlines, for example, uses its assets very productively.
Its turnaround time, or the time that its airplanes sit on the ground while they
are being unloaded and reloaded, is the lowest in the airline industry.
